From: RG35XX Java Platform
Task: RGJ-RC1-011BU
Subject: [PATCH] libretro: launch JamVM by absolute RG35XX path

This patch is applied after 0023. Real-device evidence proved javaOpen() forked
successfully and then execvp("java", ...) failed with ENOENT. The RG35XX runtime
has JamVM at /mnt/mmc/CFW/java/bin/jamvm, so remove PATH dependence while
preserving the existing argv, stdout binary video IPC, and 0023 stderr logging.

The hunks intentionally use the exact post-0023 exec/failure markers rather than
surrounding pipe-close context, so unrelated earlier process ownership remains
untouched.

--- a/src/libretro/freej2me_libretro.c
+++ b/src/libretro/freej2me_libretro.c
@@ -1836,1 +1836,6 @@
-		execvp(cmd, params);
+		const char *rg35xx_jamvm_path = "/mnt/mmc/CFW/java/bin/jamvm";
+		fprintf(stderr, "RG35XX exec JamVM path=%s argv0=%s\n",
+		        rg35xx_jamvm_path, params[0] ? params[0] : "(null)");
+		fflush(stderr);
+		execv(rg35xx_jamvm_path, params);
+
@@ -1838,2 +1843,3 @@
-		/* execvp failure! */
-		fprintf(stderr, "RG35XX execvp failed for %s: errno=%d (%s)\n", cmd, errno, strerror(errno));
+		/* execv failure! */
+		fprintf(stderr, "RG35XX execv failed for %s: errno=%d (%s)\n",
+		        rg35xx_jamvm_path, errno, strerror(errno));
